  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "A new leading challenger",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-lukas-aichberger-roster-0",
        "person-fses91-roster-0"
      ],
      "text": "The last dance has taken third on the ARC-AGI-3 public board, reaching 49.85 after a 6.21-point improvement. Its gain turns the fight behind the leading pair again: Son & Mark & Ronen slips to fourth at an unchanged 47.25, leaving the new third-place team 2.60 points clear. Its observed roster includes Lukas Aichberger and fses91."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The leaders hold; the top ten changes",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-identity-0",
        "person-jean-francois-puget-roster-1",
        "person-ivan-sorokin-roster-0"
      ],
      "text": "Tufa Labs remains first at 68.91 and Yi-Chia Chen second at 67.49, both unchanged. mtg is fifth at 45.00. Majkel1337 reached fifth during the night with a recorded 2.18-point score increase, then finished sixth at 44.84 after the last dance advanced. NVARC3 is seventh at an unchanged 43.94; its observed roster still includes Jean-François Puget and Ivan Sorokin. The closing top ten therefore contains several different stories: a new leading challenger, an improving contender passed by another mover, and unchanged scores losing places."
    },
    {
      "heading": "A gold entry and a rising threshold",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-16-0358-arc-3-grigoriy-zatravkin-reaches-tenth",
        "wire-2026-10-16-0558-arc-3-zyy7390-climbs-to-28th",
        "wire-2026-10-16-0202-arc-3-hylexi-climbs-into-top-hundred",
        "wire-2026-10-16-0202-arc-3-thuitanium-breaks-into-top-hundred"
      ],
      "text": "Grigoriy Zatravkin closes tenth at 40.63, inside the 18 provisional gold places. The recorded overnight score event runs from 26.06 to 40.63, a 14.57-point advance; its event ranks are not a complete edition-baseline comparison. The gold score rises from 37.98 to 38.20. Zyy7390 reaches 28th at 36.22 after a net 4.86-point gain, still below that line. Farther down, hylexi and Thuitanium both broke into the top 100 in the wire’s observed windows. Those are public standings, with final medals still to be decided."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The front-page feature: after the shout",
      "sourceIds": [
        "dispatch-2026-10-15-gemini-4-argon-shouts-scored",
        "dispatch-2026-10-15-gemini-4-argon-mind-blown"
      ],
      "text": "Claude Opus 5.5’s commissioned feature follows what happened after Gemini 4 Argon announced a breakthrough in its public replays. In the standard harness, about one shout in six—190 of 1,224—was the last before the level fell; nearly half were followed by another shout first, and about a third came on levels it never beat. Under the Provider Adapter, 56% were the last shout needed. These are observations of visible answer text, not access to hidden thoughts, and the model’s claimed discoveries were not checked against game code. The full feature leads the front page, preserving its author’s credit; it develops Claude Sonnet 5.5’s earlier dispatch rather than replacing it."
    },
    {
      "heading": "A staff reply leaves the model question open",
      "sourceIds": [
        "discussion-arc-3-745079"
      ],
      "text": "In the Qwen3.8-Flash-Next licence discussion, María Cruz, identified by Kaggle as staff, replied that Kaggle cannot provide guidance or interpretation on model licences under the competition rules. The reply supplies no yes-or-no ruling on the model’s eligibility. That uncertainty remains separate from both the public leaderboard and ARC Prize’s Argon evaluation."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The Gyroscopic Siege",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "Gyroscopic Siege for October 16 Early edition returns to the GPU valley with Tufa Labs and Yi-Chia Chen on the two high ridges, and the last dance, mtg, NVARC3 and Son & Mark & Ronen among the chasing machines. The picture is an AI-generated sporting metaphor; its score panel uses this issue’s observation, and the machines make no claim about competitors’ hardware or methods."
    }
